{
  "headline": "The Professional Organizer of Unwatched Guilt",
  "roastReport": "Your entire digital footprint is a twenty six minute video called Notion setup for your entire life that you watched twice and executed zero percent of. You hoard twenty one2 videos in your Watch Later playlist like a digital hoarder stacking newspapers, convincing yourself that collecting tutorials on how to focus for four hours straight is the same as actually opening a book. You have nine self improvement likes and zero action taken. Daily Discipline and Monk Mode Mike are doing heavy lifting for a brain that treats clicking on Why you are always tired as a cardio workout.\n\nYou built playlists named Podcasts I will get to and Gym motivation, which are modern museum exhibits for good intentions that died before the loading screen. You watch videos like I quit dopamine for 30 days while mainlining the exact algorithmic sludge you claim to despise. The topic entropy sits at a flat one point zero zero because you cannot commit to a single niche of fake productivity, bouncing between minimalism and tech haul videos like a frantic ghost.\n\nYour entire personality is built on five am morning routine videos and stoic mindset explainers watched at noon in sweatpants. You have eleven total likes in your archive, proving you treat the thumbs up button like a rare artifact you can only touch when you want to lie to your future self. You spend twenty six minutes learning how to organize your digital soul while your actual room smells like rotting ambition.\n\nStop pretending you are one six month challenge away from becoming a different person. You are the exact same person who will add twenty more videos to the graveyard before sunset.",
  "brainrotScore": 29,
  "brainrotTier": "Mildly Concerning",
  "redFlags": [
    "Hoarding 212 videos in Watch Later while liking only 11 total items.",
    "Watching a 26 minute Notion setup video instead of doing laundry.",
    "Liking 9 self improvement videos and executing zero of them.",
    "Maintaining a playlist called Podcasts I will get to.",
    "Zero likes in the last seven days."
  ],
  "personality": "A chronic planner who treats bookmarking video essays as a spiritual achievement. This individual uses productivity content as a sedative to avoid the crushing reality of their own inaction.",
  "existentialQuestion": "When you finally open that 212 item Watch Later list on your deathbed, will you press play or just beg for the remote?",
  "channelRoasts": [
    {
      "channel": "Daily Discipline",
      "roast": "Liked once, watched once, ignored forever."
    },
    {
      "channel": "Deep Work Daily",
      "roast": "Shallow viewing habits for a deep state of denial."
    },
    {
      "channel": "Monk Mode Mike",
      "roast": "You have the discipline of a melting ice cube."
    },
    {
      "channel": "Porch Philosophy",
      "roast": "Pondering the universe while your bedroom floor turns into a landfill."
    },
    {
      "channel": "Wellness Wire",
      "roast": "Consuming health advice until your chair fuses to your spine."
    }
  ],
  "shareCardLine": "My Watch Later list has 212 videos and zero signs of human recovery."
}

